[34m##[0m[37m [0m[34mWhat was actually wrong[0m

[37mThis[0m[37m wasn't a path[0m[37m,[0m[37m permissions, or network[0m[37m problem — it was [0m[1;33m**[0m[1;33mpartial deletion of the pip package[0m[1;33m**[0m[37m.[0m

[32m`[0m[32m/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/[0m[32m`[0m[37m contained:[0m

[37m```[0m
[37mpip-24[0m[37m.3.1.dist[0m[37m-info/[0m[37m   [0m[37m ← metadata[0m[37m:[0m[37m present[0m
[37mpip[0m[37m/[0m[37m                    [0m[37m ← actual[0m[37m code: DEL[0m[37mETED (all[0m[37m 841 files gone[0m[37m)[0m
[37m```[0m

[37mThe `pip`, `pip3`, and `pip3.13` launcher scripts in `/usr/local/bin/` still existed and were valid — they just crashed on the import:[0m

[37m```[0m
[37mFile "/usr/local/bin/pip", line 5, in <module>[0m
[37m    from pip._internal.cli.main import main[0m
[37mModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip'[0m
[37m```[0m

[1;33m**[0m[1;33mThe nasty part:[0m[1;33m**[0m[37m the leftover[0m[37m `dist-info` made[0m[37m Python believe pip[0m[37m 24.3.1[0m[37m was fully[0m[37m installed.[0m[37m So[0m[37m the[0m[37m obvious fix silently[0m[37m did[0m[37m nothing:[0m

[37m```[0m
[37m$ python[0m[37m3 -m ensurepip --[0m[37mupgrade --default-pip[0m
[37mRequirement already[0m[37m satisfied: pip in[0m[37m .../[0m[37msite-packages (24.[0m[37m3.1)[0m[37m   ←[0m[37m lied[0m[37m, installed[0m[37m nothing[0m
[37m```[0m

[37mThis is why pip can be genuinely painful to repair — the "already satisfied" check reads metadata, not the actual files.[0m

[37m## What I did[0m

[37m1. **Confirmed the diagnosis** — verified all 841 files listed in `pip`'s `RECORD` were missing, and ruled out the usual suspects (no `PIP_*`/`PYTHONPATH` env vars, no `pip.conf`, no `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` marker).[0m
[37m2. **Backed up then removed the orphaned `dist-info`** so the "already satisfied" check could no longer misfire → `/tmp/pip-orphan-dist-info-backup.tar.gz`.[0m
[37m3. **Reinstalled from the bundled wheel** with `python3 -m ensurepip --upgrade --default-pip` — this succeeded offline, no PyPI needed.[0m

